### 1. r12 mathematics — CLEAN

The five carrier degrees reconcile as follows:

| Instance | Current degree |
|---|---|
| HE3 | \(D'=e_1f_1\) |
| HE6 | \(D'=e_1f_1\) |
| HE7 | \(D''=D'\ell d_r=(e_1\ell)(f_1d_r)\) |
| HETOW | \(D_2=D'e_2f_2=(e_1e_2)(f_1f_2)\) |
| GENTOW4 | same \(D_2\) carrier as HETOW |

Strictly, the first two boxes do not independently assert \(D''=D_2\); that equality is forced at the HE7-to-tower bridge. HETOW identifies the datum by \((\ell,d_r)=(e_2,f_2)\), so

\[
D''=D'\ell d_r=D'e_2f_2=D_2.
\]

Both \(\Psi_{\kappa_2,\widetilde r}\) and \(\Phi_2\) are monic of that degree. Therefore

\[
w=\Psi_{\kappa_2,\widetilde r}-\Phi_2
\]

is zero or has \(\deg w<D''\) by leading-coefficient cancellation. The argument in the [effective r12 scope clause](/data/users/asvin/math-and-lean/p-adic-splitting-densities/lean/notes/openmath/T2_SIGMA_LADDER_MASTER_2026-08-12.md:4242) is sound.

For accumulated perturbations, every refinement increment has degree \(<D''\) by the lift bound. Hence

\[
\deg(w+w_1+\cdots+w_j)<D''
\]

whenever the sum is nonzero. This agrees byte-for-byte with HE7-12(d): “\(W:=w_1+\cdots+w_j\) has deg \(W<D''\)” at [HE7:842](/data/users/asvin/math-and-lean/p-adic-splitting-densities/lean/notes/openmath/HE7_PROOF_2026-08-08.md:842). The valuation condition is also stable: a nonzero sum of terms of value \(>T_2\) still has value \(>T_2\); if the total is zero, the unperturbed-key branch applies.

The C-A corner directive is honest. The source expressly says the literal reduced `(LIFT)` construction has “NO x-degree-\(\ge D'\) overflow” and \(w=0\) at [HETOW:213](/data/users/asvin/math-and-lean/p-adic-splitting-densities/lean/notes/openmath/HETOW_RECON_2026-08-09.md:213). C-A instead concerns a junk-augmented presentation whose moved term reaches the leading slot and makes \(w\) acquire degree at least \(D''\), at [HETOW:558](/data/users/asvin/math-and-lean/p-adic-splitting-densities/lean/notes/openmath/HETOW_RECON_2026-08-09.md:558). Such an object cannot simultaneously be the difference of the two monic degree-\(D''\) keys substituted by the instance boxes. r12 therefore correctly obeys C-A while deriving the legal \(w\ne0\) case independently.

Classification: no finding.

